SYNTHESIS
============================================================================
1. Addition is the flattening operation: as a shadow it becomes the total order x<z, but its fibers remember p+q and p+2q abundance.
2. Multiplication is the branching operation: divisors, dyadic height, and odd core build the sparse vertical skeleton under that order.
3. Product-sum equations are collision equations between those two operations: multiplication creates surplus D=P-S, and addition repairs it by D ones.
4. A000568 enters because tournament quotienting forgets labels by odd-cycle fixed-point survival; the LRC analogue must keep marked endpoint fibers over that quotient.
5. A useful loneliness metric should therefore be a stack, not one number: dynamic LRC threshold gauges, pair-cell danger, endpoint debt, odd/dyadic branch labels, and additive/product-sum fiber entropy.

Proposed practical arc criteria:
  runner level: phase_half_H, theta_close, open_arc_density, danger_deficit, pressure_relief_SCC.
  pair-cell level: edge_danger_deficit plus odd_core_row, dyadic_height_branch, product_sum_defect labels.
  denominator level: Goldbach/Lemoine scarcity, phi(N) endpoint debt, A000568 odd survival, and add_mult_gauge_stack majority.

Conjectural proof shape: a counterexample row would need to be scarce in additive fibers, high in endpoint debt, trapped in the marked A000568 fiber, and cyclic/nonpeeling in pressure gauges at the same time.
